.TH TDUWEB-CHECK-PYTHON25 1 "September 24, 2026" "darpa_spillserver 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tduweb-check-python25 \- flag Python source constructs that need Python 2.6 or later
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python2
.B contrib/tduweb/check_python25.py
.IR FILE ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
The TDU runs Python 2.5.
.B check_python25.py
scans each
.I FILE
line by line for syntax and names that arrived in 2.6 or 2.7, so a change to
.BR tdu_webserver (1)
can be checked without a 2.5 interpreter. It flags, among others:
.BR "except X as e" ,
.BR str.format() " and the " format() " builtin,"
the
.BR json ", " argparse " and " importlib
modules, bytes literals, dict and set comprehensions,
.BR OrderedDict ", " Counter ", " subprocess.check_output ,
.BR next() ", " bin() ,
.BR bytes ", " bytearray ", " memoryview ,
the
.B with
statement, and
.BR print_function .
.PP
Lines inside string literals and comments are skipped. A line ending in
.B "# py25\-ok"
is skipped too; that marks a newer name used deliberately inside a guard that
never runs on 2.5.
.PP
A source scan cannot see a name that is merely looked up at run time;
.BR tduweb-run-as-python25 (1)
covers that case.
.PP
It must itself run under Python 2, since it uses the
.B StringIO
module.
.SH OUTPUT
For each file, one line:
.IB FILE ": clean for Python 2.5"
or
.IB FILE ": " N " problem(s)" ,
followed by the line number, the reason, and the start of each offending line.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every file is clean.
.TP
.B 1
At least one problem was found.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.EX
python2 contrib/tduweb/check_python25.py \e
    contrib/tduweb/tdu_webserver.py contrib/tduweb/selftest.py
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tduweb-run-as-python25 (1),
.BR tduweb-selftest (1),
.BR tdu_webserver (1)
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report defects at
\fBhttps://github.com/NovaDAQ/TDUWeb/issues\fR.
.SH AUTHOR
NOvA DAQ group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
